#2500
The Edge Of The Mistwood~
   The trail from the copse ends here against a wall of grey mist that does
not move with the wind. Old trees stand half-seen inside it, their bark pale
as bone. A post of black iron is driven into the ground at the edge, hung
with a board. The air is cold and smells faintly of struck flint. A narrow
path goes north into the mist; the copse lies back to the south.
~
