#2501
The Mistwood~
   The mist is thick enough to taste. Grey trunks crowd in on every side,
and a ring of white stones has been laid on the ground here, as if to mark a
place where something was buried, or where something should stay. Faint
growling comes from nowhere in particular. Paths, or what may be paths, lead
north, east, south and west.
~
